# One line-ending rule for the repository, whatever core.autocrlf says on the machine: text is
# stored and checked out with LF (PowerShell 5.1 and 7, Python and the browser all read LF), except
# batch files, which cmd.exe needs in CRLF. This is what stops git's "CRLF will be replaced by LF"
# warnings: the working tree matches what git stores.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.7z binary
